# Session interactive-first mindset (Gamification & Animated Diagrams)

**Every concept gets an animation or interactive diagram. Static bullet points are not slides — they are notes.**

When you are asked about a GenAI/CS concept in the context of preparing a session, your **first instinct** must be:

> "How do I show this with a step-through animation or interactive diagram — not how do I write text about it?"

---

## The rule in one sentence

If a concept can be shown, it must be shown. Text alone is a fallback of last resort.

---

## Decision flow when planning a concept slide

```
1. What is the one core idea to teach on this slide?
        ↓
2. Does the component gallery already have something that fits?
   → YES  →  Reuse it (wire the right props). Do not build a new one.
   → NO   →  Design a new interactive component (see "Component design principles" below).
        ↓
3. The result is one animated/interactive component per slide (one ## heading).
   Never add explanatory paragraph text below the title.
```

---

## Component gallery — check this FIRST

`docs/component-gallery.md` is the authoritative catalog. Before building anything, scan the "Quick chooser" table for the teaching need that matches your concept.

### Common concept → component mappings

| Teaching need | Prefer |
|---|---|
| **First slide / session outline (mandatory)** | `SessionOutlineSlide` — items auto-injected from frontmatter `outline` field; no MDX props needed |
| Multi-step process / pipeline | `NodeFlowDiagram`, `MacroPipeline`, `DualLanePipelineDiagram` |
| Before vs After / Compare two ideas | `ConceptCompare`, `ArchitectureComparisonDemo` |
| Numbered phases / story | `StepSequence` (narrative), `ConceptStepper` |
| Slider / dial affects output | `ParameterSlider`, `TokenProbDist` |
| Something that builds over time (token-by-token, step-by-step) | `AutoregressiveDemo`, `StepSequence`, `AgentLoopStepper` |
| Math / geometry / vectors | `CosineSimilarityExplorer`, `EmbeddingVectorExplorer`, `Vector2DPlot` |
| Algorithm / data-structure walkthrough | `AlgorithmStepper`, `BTreeExplorer`, `CallStackVisualizer` |
| Network / flow / packet | `ApiLifecycleFlow`, `PacketJourneyVisualizer`, `NodeFlowDiagram` |
| Training / loss / gradients | `GradientDescentSimulator`, `LinearRegressionTrainingExplorer`, `TrainingLoopSimulator` |
| Model internals (Transformer) | `TransformerPipelineWalkthrough`, `SelfAttentionScoreExplorer`, `TransformerSubstackExplorer` |
| Code that evolves | `CodeEvolutionStepper`, `AnnotatedCode`, `TabbedCodeExplorer` |
| User interacts with live input | `LiveTokenizer`, `BytePairEncodingExplorer`, `SearchQuerySimulator`, `MiniPlayground` |
| Simulation / race / concurrent state | `MutexRaceDetector`, `ConsensusSimulator`, `MessageQueueSim`, `ProcessSchedulerViz` |
| RNN / CNN / architecture story | `ArchitectureEvolutionAnimator` (panel prop for one slide), `RNNWorkingExample`, `FNNAutocompleteDemo` |

